## 6 — Activation posture: what the data licenses

HADF v7.0 shipped inert (`enabled: false`) as a `hardware_context` *input* to the
existing v5.2/v6.0 dispatch engine — Extension-not-Replacement. A three-band
confidence gate governs effect: **< 0.4** ignored (dispatch bit-for-bit identical
to v5.2, zero regression); **0.4–0.7** advisory only; **> 0.7** hardware scores
multiply routing weights.

**Licensed now by closed data:** a **scoped partial activation** — flip the
cloud-provider discrimination modifier into the >0.7 band (silhouette 0.7003 @
k=5 defensibly clears it), and keep the device-local and routing-layer modifiers
≤0.7 (advisory) until Sub-exps 2 & 3 close. The zero-regression gate guarantees
the staged flip carries no risk to the system-wide guardrails (crash-free >99.5%,
dispatch unchanged below threshold).

